Other space discretization methods. When the finite difference formulas above are used to solve a problem, the space (or ζ -) discretization is held fixed throughout the solution. This is not the most desirable strategy when rapid spatial variations occur only in some portions of the problem, because the (fixed) discretization must be appropriately refined to capture these variations, but might be needlessly fine everywhere else. A growing body of research has addressed the issue of adaptive space discretizations, and is reviewed in Ref. 21. Because of the simplicity of the PDE studied in this paper, however, no such discretization scheme will be considered here.
